  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Awadesh Kumar vs State Of U.P. on 22 May, 2020 Author: Siddharth Bench: Siddharth High Court Of Judicature At Allahabad ?In Chamber Case :- Criminal Misc. Bail Application No. - 12798 of 2020 Applicant :- Awadesh Kumar Opposite Party :- State of U.P. Counsel for Applicant :- Pradeep Yadav Counsel for Opposite Party :- G.A. Hon'ble Siddharth,J.",
    "facts": "Offence under section 60, 63, 72 of Excise Act is bailable and trible by Magistrate.",
    "arguments": "Heard Shri Pradeep Yadav, learned counsel for the applicant through Video Conferencing. Submission is that Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006 has been enacted by the legislature and hence the implication of the applicant under section 272, 273 I.P.C. is unjustified. False recovery has been alleged. The applicant is languishing in jail since 6.1.2020.The applicant Keeping in view the nature of the offence, evidence on record regarding complicity of the accused, larger mandate of the Article 21 of the Constitution of India and the dictum of Apex Court in the case of Dataram Singh Vs. State of U.P. and another reported in (2018)3 SCC 22",
    "petitioner_arguments": "Heard Shri Pradeep Yadav, learned counsel for the applicant through Video Conferencing. Submission is that Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006 has been enacted by the legislature and hence the implication of the applicant under section 272, 273 I.P.C. is unjustified. The applicant is languishing in jail since 6.1.2020.The applicant",
    "respondent_arguments": "False recovery has been alleged.",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": "Keeping in view the nature of the offence, evidence on record regarding complicity of the accused, larger mandate of the Article 21 of the Constitution of India and the dictum of Apex Court in the case of Dataram Singh Vs. State of U.P. and another reported in (2018)3 SCC 22"
  },
